=[ Telaion ]

Themeless Svelte 5 components for editing Tomet documents. The frame that Tomet editors are built on.

==[ Overview ]

Telaion keeps the parts that every Tomet editor needs in one place, so that an editor is assembled instead of rewritten. Its name derives from *telaio*, the Italian word for a loom or a frame: it carries structure and behavior, and leaves the look to the application.

==[ Packages ]

-| `@telaion/primitives` -- Themeless primitives and design tokens. Knows nothing about Tomet.
-| `@telaion/editor` -- The editor frame: content in, content out, and a storage adapter for loading and saving. The language is a plug-in slot.
-| `@telaion/tomet` -- The Tomet-specific parts of an editor: syntax highlighting, conflict blocks and their resolution. It knows what a highlight span or a conflict looks like, but it carries no Tomet engine: the application supplies one.

The design is written down in @dir(tmtroot/design/).

==[ Development ]

===[ Prerequisites ]

- Nix with Flakes enabled (recommended)
- Node.js & pnpm

===[ Using Nix Flake ]

```bash
direnv allow
# or
nix develop
```

===[ Setup ]

```bash
just install
```

===[ Looking at the components ]

```bash
just play    # the playground, with hot reload
just test    # browser tests against the playground
just check   # type-check
```

